{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "36db6e5b-d64f-4051-8c6b-c7a655907ecc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 1. What is python ?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b9411aa6-f211-45e8-b02c-a44d8e706cbc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "python is a high level,genreal-purpose programming language known for its simple, readable syntax that closely resembles plain english."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "26d06220-8c8d-4e83-9053-ef4addf9d09d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 2. In which areas python is used ?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c3867616-1751-443a-9a14-499d5d178636",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Web development \n",
    "\n",
    "Artifical intelligence(AI) \n",
    "\n",
    "Machine learning \n",
    "\n",
    "Data Science\n",
    "\n",
    "Automation\n",
    "\n",
    "Software Devlopment"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f1be9a38-25dc-49c0-a12c-1683819fa032",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 3. what are high-level and low-level languages ?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2afd96f2-2255-4d4c-b4b9-a5477c50170a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "High-level language :- Easy for humans to read and understand. e.g.:- python\n",
    "\n",
    "Low-level language :- Closer to computer hardware. e.g. :- Assembly langauge"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4b699d5f-feb0-4e5d-be10-228f32250f0a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 4. what are interpreted and compiled langauages ?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fa4aaebd-24fc-40c1-b5ad-436d96c322b5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Interpreted language :- A language whose entire code executed at run-time by an interpreter. e.g. :- python\n",
    "\n",
    "Compiled language :- Whose entire source code converted into machine code before execution. e.g. :- c"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e5c9b9f7-5951-4f83-992c-93b5bee93fc1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 5. what are staticslly and dynamically typed languages ?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4ebc24d3-99fd-45b3-9815-3516dd8cc440",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Statically typed :- A programming language in which variable data types are known and checked before executing code. e.g. :- C\n",
    "\n",
    "Dynamically typed :-  A programming language in which variable data types are determined and checked while executing the code. e.g. :- python"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "62c28a25-3915-49e9-84a8-3568d2d1be21",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 6. what are weakly and strongly typed lanuages ?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b3909f5a-a9d4-47b9-9d5a-449bc607dc5d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Strongly typed :-  Programming language that strictly enforces data type rules, preventing operations between incompatible types. e.g. :- python\n",
    "\n",
    "Weakly typed :- Programming language that automatically converts incompatible data types behind the scenes so operations can proceed without throwing an error.. e.g. :- JavaScript"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ea741923-3790-4c34-ab9d-87d61a449dd1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 7. what is a .PYC file (Byte code) when it is created? ?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "16a79f84-24a1-4e16-8ddb-70eb18906f34",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "A .pyc file is compiled bytecode of python interpreter and it is created automatically when importing module into another programme."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5c5dc487-fa79-4821-984e-96de335b99a5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 8. What is PVM ?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e2137023-b793-4c8a-a6fc-54466513c613",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "PVM (Python Virtual Machine) is the runtime engine of Python that reads compiled bytecode."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9aba6606-231d-475d-b29e-d1e6e9b732e6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 9. How does Python works internally ?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "49f91855-c8d8-4e33-90d8-aad547c9038d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "                    _________Interpreter________\n",
    "Code editor --> Source code (.py) --> Compiler --> Bytecode (.pyc) --> PVM --> Output"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "530b1c81-28ed-498e-b26b-fc5406e4d041",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 10. What is PEP 8 ?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a24be87f-fce1-4f5e-b1e6-52b8b4cb3252",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "PEP 8 is the official python guide line written by its createor GUDIO VAN ROSSUM."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5ddf3b56-06c1-4cfc-a0f8-278597e5a29d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 11. What is PIP ? What is its use ?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bae65ff7-32e1-4c5f-a7ea-adaef0556534",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "PIP stands for PIP INSTALLS PACKAGES. It is used to update and unistall python libraries.\n",
    "\n",
    "e.g. :- pip install numpy install the numpy liabrary."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "025e43df-2250-463b-bbbe-bc58dbb2298f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 12. What is __pycache__folder ?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6d7110a3-c222-4875-a7ac-2e0fa86140b3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The __pycache__ folder is a directory automatically created by Python to store compiled bytecode files (.pyc) of your imported Python modules."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b3792523-e227-49da-bf11-332ce2f1d448",
